1
00:00:00,908 --> 00:00:02,408
(Sheldon:)of quantum mechanics?

2
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:04,480
(Howard:)Since every interpretation gives
exactly the same answer

3
00:00:04,479 --> 00:00:06,409
(Howard:)to every measurement,
they are all equally correct.

4
00:00:06,414 --> 00:00:08,614
(Howard:)However, I know you believe in
the Many Worlds Interpretation,

5
00:00:08,616 --> 00:00:11,186
(Howard:)so I'll say that. Now do you
think I'm smart enough?

6
00:00:14,555 --> 00:00:16,125
(chuckles):
No.

7
00:00:17,758 --> 00:00:19,458
(Howard:)Oh, come on.
You might've gone to school

8
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:21,530
(Howard:)for a couple more years than me,
but guess what--

9
00:00:21,529 --> 00:00:23,599
(Howard:)engineers are just
as smart as physicists.

10
00:00:23,598 --> 00:00:25,898
(gasps)
You take that back!

11
00:00:29,036 --> 00:00:31,536
(mimicking Sheldon):
No.

12
00:00:36,444 --> 00:00:37,914
(Amy:)So, after drinks
with Bernadette,

13
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:40,842
(Amy:)I get home, and Penny calls
to complain about her.

14
00:00:40,848 --> 00:00:42,478
(Amy:)And then while
I'm talking to Penny,

15
00:00:42,483 --> 00:00:43,983
(Amy:)I get a text from Bernadette.

16
00:00:43,985 --> 00:00:46,985
Wh... I'm trying to prepare
my lesson plan for Howard.

17
00:00:46,988 --> 00:00:49,988
(Sheldon:)Why are you
telling me this?

18
00:00:49,991 --> 00:00:54,031
(Amy:)Because it's taken 15 years, but
high school is finally awesome!

19
00:00:56,030 --> 00:00:57,760
(Amy:)I love them both,

20
00:00:57,765 --> 00:01:01,735
but I'm in the center now,
and I love that even more.

